<worksheet xml:id="LinearAlgebraExam1Page3" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title> Linear Algebra Sample Exam 1A - PAGE 3 </title>
    
<page>
    <p>  5. (2 points) Write down the solutions to <m> A\vec{x} = \vec{b}</m> in parametric vector form. 
    You do not need to show your work. </p>

    <me>
  A = \begin{pmatrix}
    0 &amp; 2 &amp; 0 &amp; 4 &amp; 0 \\
    0 &amp; 0 &amp; 1 &amp; -5 &amp; 0 \\
    0 &amp; 0 &amp; 0 &amp; 0 &amp; 3
  \end{pmatrix}, \quad 
  \vec{b} = \begin{pmatrix}
    6 \\
    4 \\
    3
  \end{pmatrix}
</me>



<p>
  <m>\rule{0pt}{5cm}</m> 
</p>

<p>  6. (2 points) Please show your work for this question.</p>
<p> Construct a linear system and use row reductions to determine a non zero choice
of <m> a, b, c, d</m> so that the circle below passes through the points <m> P(1,0), Q(0,-2), </m> and <m> R(0,0).</m>  Please show work. </p>
<p> <me> a(x^2 + y^2) + bx + cy + d = 0 </me> </p>




</page>

  
  
